    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nbase16, hues\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nBy default, \"LeapMatch\" uses underline as visual cue to help us predict whether we'll need an additional label. This is currently overridden by both Mini.Hues and Mini.Base16, which opt to use bold green instead which is not always apparent, especially considering potential changes in hues:\r\n\r\n![Screenshot from 2024-01-16 14-38-12](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/91024200/732ed965-ae70-4f01-9b50-0d231e2054b2)\r\n![Screenshot from 2024-01-16 14-38-18](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/91024200/5da6be7f-28c3-4be6-8b7e-cc733f43cd00)\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWith Leap's intended default underline, it becomes much clearer:\r\n\r\n![Screenshot from 2024-01-16 14-43-44](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/91024200/aa360297-26ea-43a3-a966-0f69b188740f)\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/91024200/afd6f9e2-764e-418e-8441-030360d7e6dd)\r\n\r\n\r\n### Neovim version\r\n\r\nNVIM v0.10.0-dev+1974-g714b07519\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n1. `nvim -nu minimal.lua`\r\n2. set `highlight_unlabeled_phase_one_targets = true` in leap's options.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n### Expected behavior\r\n\r\nPreserve Leap defaults attributes.\r\n\r\n### Actual behavior\r\n\r\nAttributes are overwritten.",
