            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> Thanks! I already did so prior to opening this issue. In fact, I pondered whether opening an issue was worth it. However, in the end, I concluded that color should not take precedence over plugin-intended attributes, so I decided to proceed-\r\n\r\nNo harm in opening an issue if you did spend time to think if it was worth it :)\r\n\r\nI don't think underline *is* a plugin-intended attribute, because it is not documented. What plugins define in their code is default highlighting which would be applied if there is no definition by user or color scheme. So it is more of a reference for color scheme authors.",
